    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e2",
      "status": "PRESENT",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "The follow‑up endoscopy rate (FER), which encompass procedures like colonoscopy or flexible sigmoidoscopy, greatly influence the economic viability of CCE. In addition to its economic effects, FER influences patient experiences and environmental sustainability. ... This systematic review and meta‑analysis aim to evaluate FERs and identify factors influencing these rates to support the effective implementation of CCE.",
      "reason": "The passage explicitly explains why the review is needed: FER impacts cost‑effectiveness, patient experience, and environmental sustainability, justifying the conduct of the review."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e3",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "Despite its significance, a systematic review of FER in CCE remains absent.",
      "reason": "The authors state that no prior systematic review on FER in CCE exists, so the conditional requirement to discuss existing similar reviews does not apply."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e4",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_5",
      "quote": "The primary aim of the review was to evaluate the FER following CCE. The secondary aims include exploring contributing factors to the FER to guide future research to reduce this rate further.",
      "reason": "The review focuses on diagnostic performance and follow‑up rates, not on the effects of an intervention; therefore, describing a mechanism of action is not applicable."
    },
    {
      "element_id": "prisma_2020_3_e5",
      "status": "NOT_APPLICABLE",
      "chunk_id": "text_4",
      "quote": "",
      "reason": "No logic model or hypothesised relationships between intervention components and outcomes are presented in the introduction, and the review does not involve a complex intervention requiring such a model."
    }
  ],
  "confidence": 95
}

